    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#transaction-path",
      "name": "Mike Ye M&A transaction path",
      "description": "Seven ordered transaction stages; the ten M&A knowledge pillars are a separate subject taxonomy.",
      "itemListOrder": "https://schema.org/ItemListOrderAscending",
      "numberOfItems": 7,
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "item": {
            "@type": "CreativeWork",
            "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#stage-mandate",
            "name": "Mandate",
            "description": "Why acquire instead of build, partner, or do nothing? Evidence: A defined business need, capital envelope, risk limits, executive sponsor, and decision authority. Judgment: Frame before detail. The target must serve the mandate. Decision gates: Gate 0 · Mandate approved.",
            "isPartOf": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#transaction-path"
            },
            "hasPart": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/ma-resources/ma-deal-workflow-checklist#resource"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "item": {
            "@type": "CreativeWork",
            "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#stage-thesis-targets",
            "name": "Thesis & Targets",
            "description": "What must be true, and which targets fit and can actually be bought? Evidence: Thesis conditions, ranked target screen, pass rationale, ownership map, control path, and initial downside test. Judgment: Underwrite rather than admire. Strategic appeal does not establish transactability. Decision gates: Gates 1–2 · Thesis and target approved.",
            "isPartOf": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#transaction-path"
            },
            "hasPart": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/ma-resources/ma-deal-workflow-checklist#resource"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 3,
          "item": {
            "@type": "CreativeWork",
            "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#stage-first-look-underwriting",
            "name": "First Look & Underwriting",
            "description": "Do access, standalone economics, financing, and downside support a bid? Evidence: Minimum information package, reconstructed financials, valuation range, financing case, and private price ceiling. Judgment: Replicate the financials. Keep buyer-created synergy separate from standalone value. Decision gates: Gates 3–4 · Access and economics approved.",
            "isPartOf": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#transaction-path"
            },
            "hasPart": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/tools-and-models#webpage"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 4,
          "item": {
            "@type": "CreativeWork",
            "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#stage-loi-diligence",
            "name": "LOI & Diligence",
            "description": "Are core terms clear, and can the team test the conditions behind the thesis? Evidence: Approved LOI, evidence requests, workflow tests, accountable workstream owners, and a live issue log. Judgment: Unknowns are findings. Give each material issue a consequence: Investigate, Price, Protect, or Walk. Decision gates: Gates 5–6 · Exclusivity approved and diligence launched.",
            "isPartOf": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#transaction-path"
            },
            "hasPart": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/ma-resources/before-you-buy-follow-the-work#resource"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 5,
          "item": {
            "@type": "CreativeWork",
            "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#stage-re-underwrite-sign",
            "name": "Re-underwrite & Sign",
            "description": "Does the deal still work on the facts and terms now in front of the buyer? Evidence: Revised valuation and synergy case, combined downside, final economics, protections, closing conditions, and integration owners. Judgment: Re-establish the price ceiling before signing. Prior spending does not justify the next commitment. Decision gates: Gates 7–8 · Re-underwriting and signing approved.",
            "isPartOf": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#transaction-path"
            },
            "hasPart": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/ma-resources/synergy-underwriting-value-bridge#resource"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 6,
          "item": {
            "@type": "CreativeWork",
            "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#stage-close-day-one",
            "name": "Close & Day 1",
            "description": "Can funds and control transfer while the business keeps working? Evidence: Funds flow, required consents and clearances, closing checklist, and customer, cash, people, and system readiness. Judgment: Protect revenue while integrating cost. Do not confuse signing with operating readiness. Decision gates: Gates 9–10 · Closing approved and Day 1 stable.",
            "isPartOf": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#transaction-path"
            },
            "hasPart": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/ma-resources/after-the-deal-keep-the-business-working#resource"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 7,
          "item": {
            "@type": "CreativeWork",
            "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#stage-value-delivery-review",
            "name": "Value Delivery & Review",
            "description": "Has the buyer delivered the underwritten value, and what should change next time? Evidence: 30/60/100-day reviews, realized cash benefits and costs, workflow decisions, revised forecasts, and residual action owners. Judgment: Compare results with the original thesis. A synergy belongs in the results only when the operating work delivers it. Decision gates: Gates 11–12 · Value delivery confirmed and program closed.",
            "isPartOf": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/m-and-a#transaction-path"
            },
            "hasPart": {
              "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/ma-resources/synergy-underwriting-value-bridge#resource"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
